<article class="env-lemma" id="0BMG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BMG">Lemma <span data-tag="0BMG">9.16.5</span>.</a> Let $L/K$ be an algebraic normal extension. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $L/M/K$ is a subextension with $M/K$ finite, then there exists a tower $L/M'/M/K$ with $M'/K$ finite and normal. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $L/M'/M/K$ is a tower with $M/K$ normal and $M'/M$ finite, then there exists a tower $L/M''/M'/M/K$ with $M''/M$ finite and $M''/K$ normal. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Proof of (1). Let $M'$ be the smallest subextension of $L/K$ containing $M$ which is normal over $K$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/09DT" data-tag="09DT">9.16.3</a> this is the normal closure of $M/K$ and is finite over $K$. 
    <p>
      Proof of (2). Let $\alpha _1, \ldots , \alpha _ n \in M'$ generate $M'$ over $M$. Let $P_1, \ldots , P_ n$ be the minimal polynomials of $\alpha _1, \ldots , \alpha _ n$ over $K$. Let $\alpha _{i, j}$ be the roots of $P_ i$ in $L$. Let $M'' = M(\alpha _{i, j})$. It follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BR3" data-tag="0BR3">9.15.6</a> (applied with the set of generators $M \cup \{ \alpha _{i, j}\} $) that $M''$ is normal over $K$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>